{"documentCount":11,"nextId":11,"documentIds":{"0":"getting-started/introduction","1":"getting-started/introduction#overview","2":"getting-started/introduction#key-features","3":"reference/formatting-demo","4":"reference/formatting-demo#callout-variations","5":"reference/formatting-demo#code-block-syntax-highlighting","6":"reference/formatting-demo#gfm-markdown-table","7":"servers/network-access","8":"servers/network-access#lan-vs-public-hosting","9":"servers/network-access#firewall-configuration","10":"servers/network-access#connection-security"},"fieldIds":{"docTitle":0,"heading":1,"content":2},"fieldLength":{"0":[1,1,32],"1":[1,1,36],"2":[1,2,44],"3":[2,2,34],"4":[2,2,50],"5":[2,4,17],"6":[2,3,60],"7":[4,4,38],"8":[4,4,52],"9":[4,2,32],"10":[4,2,52]},"averageFieldLength":[2.4545454545454546,2.4545454545454546,40.63636363636363],"storedFields":{"0":{"id":"getting-started/introduction","docTitle":"Introduction","heading":"Introduction","group":"getting-started","path":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","content":"Welcome to StrataLauncher documentation! StrataLauncher is an open source, high performance launcher engineered for Minecraft: Java Edition. Overview This documentation site provides setup guides, network troubleshooting steps, and technical references for developers and players alike. <Note"},"1":{"id":"getting-started/introduction#overview","docTitle":"Introduction","heading":"Overview","group":"getting-started","path":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#overview","content":"This documentation site provides setup guides, network troubleshooting steps, and technical references for developers and players alike. <Note title=\"Hobby Project\" StrataLauncher is a non commercial community project and is not affiliated with Mojang Studios or Microsoft. </Note"},"2":{"id":"getting-started/introduction#key-features","docTitle":"Introduction","heading":"Key Features","group":"getting-started","path":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#key-features","content":"Blazing Fast Startup : Native desktop UI designed for smooth performance and responsive navigation. Multiple Instance Management : Easily manage isolated versions, mods, and mod loaders. Modern Security : Safe local credential storage and compliant authentication workflows. Continue to our server network access guide or see our formatting reference."},"3":{"id":"reference/formatting-demo","docTitle":"Formatting Demo","heading":"Formatting Demo","group":"reference","path":"/docs/reference/formatting-demo","content":"This page demonstrates the styling capabilities of the StrataLauncher documentation shell, including code blocks, GFM tables, and callouts. Callout Variations Here is an example of each callout component: <Note title=\"Documentation Note\" This is an informative note callout highlighting ne"},"4":{"id":"reference/formatting-demo#callout-variations","docTitle":"Formatting Demo","heading":"Callout Variations","group":"reference","path":"/docs/reference/formatting-demo#callout-variations","content":"Here is an example of each callout component: <Note title=\"Documentation Note\" This is an informative note callout highlighting neutral background context or additional tips. </Note <Tip title=\"Pro Tip\" Tips provide recommendations for enhanced performance, workflow speed, or best practices. </Tip <Warning title=\"System Warning\" Warnings alert users to potential configuration errors, security risks, or breaking changes. </Warning"},"5":{"id":"reference/formatting-demo#code-block-syntax-highlighting","docTitle":"Formatting Demo","heading":"Code Block Syntax Highlighting","group":"reference","path":"/docs/reference/formatting-demo#code-block-syntax-highlighting","content":"Below are code blocks demonstrating dual theme highlighting via Shiki with copy buttons and language labels."},"6":{"id":"reference/formatting-demo#gfm-markdown-table","docTitle":"Formatting Demo","heading":"GFM Markdown Table","group":"reference","path":"/docs/reference/formatting-demo#gfm-markdown-table","content":"The table below verifies GitHub Flavored Markdown table parsing and styling: Setting Key Default Value Description : : : maxMemoryMb 4096 Maximum heap allocation allocated to the JVM enableVsync true Matches rendering refresh rate to primary monitor customJavaPath null Optional override path to a custom Java installation reducedMotion false Disables non essential launcher interface animations All table borders, headers, and rows adapt seamlessly across light and dark themes."},"7":{"id":"servers/network-access","docTitle":"Network Access & Server Hosting","heading":"Network Access & Server Hosting","group":"servers","path":"/docs/servers/network-access","content":"When configuring a Minecraft server or connecting with friends in StrataLauncher, appropriate network configurations ensure reliable and secure gameplay. LAN vs Public Hosting Local Area Network (LAN) games broadcast automatically across your immediate local subnet without port forwarding. `"},"8":{"id":"servers/network-access#lan-vs-public-hosting","docTitle":"Network Access & Server Hosting","heading":"LAN vs Public Hosting","group":"servers","path":"/docs/servers/network-access#lan-vs-public-hosting","content":"Local Area Network (LAN) games broadcast automatically across your immediate local subnet without port forwarding. Public hosting requires exposing a port (default 25565) to the WAN or utilizing an encrypted tunneling service. <Tip title=\"LAN Broadcast Tip\" Ensure all players on a local network are connected to the same wireless SSID or switch before attempting direct IP connections. </Tip"},"9":{"id":"servers/network-access#firewall-configuration","docTitle":"Network Access & Server Hosting","heading":"Firewall Configuration","group":"servers","path":"/docs/servers/network-access#firewall-configuration","content":"Host operating systems typically block incoming connections on port 25565 by default. On Windows and macOS, verify that the Java runtime or launcher executable is granted permission through the system defender firewall."},"10":{"id":"servers/network-access#connection-security","docTitle":"Network Access & Server Hosting","heading":"Connection Security","group":"servers","path":"/docs/servers/network-access#connection-security","content":"When opening server ports to the wider Internet, security considerations must be observed. <Warning title=\"Security Advisory\" Never share your public IP address publicly without protection. Use whitelisting and enforce strong online mode authentication in your server configuration. </Warning Always keep your instance mods and server jars updated to the latest stable versions to protect against known exploits."}},"dirtCount":0,"index":[["known",{"2":{"10":1}}],["keep",{"2":{"10":1}}],["key",{"1":{"2":1},"2":{"6":1}}],["25565",{"2":{"8":1,"9":1}}],["`",{"2":{"7":1}}],["your",{"2":{"7":1,"8":1,"10":3}}],["jars",{"2":{"10":1}}],["java",{"2":{"0":1,"6":1,"9":1}}],["jvm",{"2":{"6":1}}],["4096",{"2":{"6":1}}],["runtime",{"2":{"9":1}}],["rows",{"2":{"6":1}}],["rate",{"2":{"6":1}}],["risks",{"2":{"4":1}}],["requires",{"2":{"8":1}}],["reliable",{"2":{"7":1}}],["reducedmotion",{"2":{"6":1}}],["refresh",{"2":{"6":1}}],["reference",{"2":{"2":1}}],["references",{"2":{"0":1,"1":1}}],["rendering",{"2":{"6":1}}],["recommendations",{"2":{"4":1}}],["responsive",{"2":{"2":1}}],["updated",{"2":{"10":1}}],["use",{"2":{"10":1}}],["users",{"2":{"4":1}}],["utilizing",{"2":{"8":1}}],["ui",{"2":{"2":1}}],["by",{"2":{"9":1}}],["broadcast",{"2":{"7":1,"8":2}}],["breaking",{"2":{"4":1}}],["borders",{"2":{"6":1}}],["buttons",{"2":{"5":1}}],["be",{"2":{"10":1}}],["before",{"2":{"8":1}}],["below",{"2":{"5":1,"6":1}}],["best",{"2":{"4":1}}],["background",{"2":{"4":1}}],["block",{"1":{"5":1},"2":{"9":1}}],["blocks",{"2":{"3":1,"5":1}}],["blazing",{"2":{"2":1}}],["vs",{"1":{"8":1},"2":{"7":1}}],["value",{"2":{"6":1}}],["variations",{"1":{"4":1},"2":{"3":1}}],["verify",{"2":{"9":1}}],["verifies",{"2":{"6":1}}],["version